    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23e4751f_fead8ba4",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1802,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T07:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This came up in the meeting as well.\nIt is a good thing and desirable that we disable the chain in any previous release, since NPMS code using it will be absent and we don\u0027t want any problematic or unintentional use by OEMs.",
      "parentUuid": "00e0509b_cbd8ef34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1802,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1802,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52044055_3f99325b",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1802,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T11:20:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought we added FIREWALL_CHAIN_BACKGROUND to sdk extension since we want to use this before V.\nNPMS does not set background firewall chain on 24Q2?\nIf no, it\u0027s fine. I just want to confirm.",
      "parentUuid": "23e4751f_fead8ba4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1802,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1802,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e8da589_c91d4962",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1802,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T02:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We wanted to but it got postponed to V due to various process and technical reasons. There is no code in the framework that should call this API before VIC.",
      "parentUuid": "52044055_3f99325b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1802,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1802,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd8b5caf_52c86ed0",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13599,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-27T09:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s better to add check in `setUidFirewallRule` and `replaceFirewallChain` as well.\nThis is not necessary since uid rule is not used if chain is not enabled.\nBut as a kill swtich, I feel it would be safer not to write BACKGROUND_MATCH to any bpf map if mBackgroundFirewallChainEnabled is false.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13599,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 13599,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e572419b_242bf4cf",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13599,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T07:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about this a bit. And TBH it feels scarier to me to disable any code that adds BACKGROUND_MATCH to any uids, because this is an allowlist chain.\n\nIf the chain stays disabled - the behavior we want, all is good. \n*But* if any other code accidentally enables the chain at any time after boot, then we will be stuck in a state where 0 apps can access the network -- even the ones in foreground.\n\nHaving such an obvious failure mode may be preferable -- if you are 100% sure that such a scenario can never happen and if it happens, then there is a fast path to fix the issue on users devices in the field.\n\nSo if you insist I can guard those code paths as well. But IMO this is safer.",
      "parentUuid": "dd8b5caf_52c86ed0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13599,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 13599,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9036a12a_47301a9b",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13599,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T09:11:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I just tweaked it to only ignore `enable` calls. Let me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "e572419b_242bf4cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13599,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 13599,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d9a139f_9336a251",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13599,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T11:20:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is bug in ConnectivityService code that handles background chain(e.g. code that write value to bpf map, actual bpf code)\n\nIn ConnectivityService, we usually use kill switch flag to disable whole feature since we don\u0027t know which code could have the issue.\n\nSo I still prefer not to do anything if mBackgroundFirewallChainEnabled is false and chain is FIREWALL_CHAIN_BACKGROUND.\nAnd I don\u0027t think apps can modify bpfMap without calling `setFirewallChainEnabled`, `setUidFirewallRule`, or `replaceFirewallChain`.\n\nBTW, If we enable mBackgroundFirewallChainEnabled only on V+, do we need kill switch?\nDo you worry that we will find the issue only after we start shipping V devices?",
      "parentUuid": "9036a12a_47301a9b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13599,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 13599,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "10a7e4fbaad6a51135dbc57d9c101e5a70c990e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd3af441_8f53748e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13599,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T02:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This flag is specifically meant for (a) killing the feature in emergency, (b) experimenting on Beta or small populations to isolate exact impact to battery and performance metrics.\n\nSince the feature is only meant to work on V, we need to enable both (a) and (b) on VIC. For earlier versions we just want to explicitly disable the code.\n\nI will follow your recommendation and disable any and all modifications for this chain.",
      "parentUuid": "3d9a139f_9336a251",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13599,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 13599,
        "endChar": 19
      },
